{
  "schema": "kp.openpbr.library/1",
  "openpbrVersion": "1.1",
  "_comment": [
    "Mirrors the 19 MaterialDefs in src/model/materials.ts (never rename an id",
    "— it is persisted in designs). `appColor` is the def's own `color` hex;",
    "`tileMeters` mirrors src/view3d/textures.ts TILE_M (null for pattern",
    "'none'). `openpbr` lists only params that deviate from the OpenPBR 1.1",
    "spec defaults, plus base_color and specular_roughness which are always",
    "present. `textureSet.tint` is the multiplier applied ON TOP of the",
    "sampled texture, as a float triple: baseColorMode 'multiply' uses the",
    "material's own appColor-derived tone as tint, so several species can",
    "share one photographed grain/roughness/normal set and still land on the",
    "right hue (`base_color = texture_sample * tint`); baseColorMode 'asis'",
    "means the texture's own colour is used unmodified and tint is the",
    "neutral [1,1,1] no-op (kept for shape uniformity). 'replace' is reserved",
    "for a future case where a flat tint should override the sampled colour",
    "entirely; no entry below uses it yet. Glass and the two plastics have no",
    "textureSet — they render from flat OpenPBR params only, same as the",
    "procedural three.js path for pattern 'none'."
  ],
